<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Finding your way around">
        <FluentText>
            The <a href="/manage/rota">Rota Builder</a> shows a row for each person who holds a position at the
            location. Use the arrows and <strong>Today</strong> to move around, and <strong>Week</strong> or
            <strong>Month</strong> to change the view. On a phone it shows one day at a time. Tick
            <strong>Show staff without a position</strong> to include everyone at the location.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding and changing shifts">
        <ol>
            <li>Click an empty cell to add a shift, or an existing shift to change it.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Staff member</strong>, or <strong>Open shift (anyone can pick it up)</strong>
                to offer it to whoever can work it.</li>
            <li>Set the <strong>Date</strong>, <strong>Start</strong>, <strong>End</strong>, <strong>Unpaid break
                (minutes)</strong>, <strong>Position</strong> and any <strong>Notes</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Save</strong>, or <strong>Save &amp; add another</strong> to keep going.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Not sure who to use? Select <strong>Suggest staff</strong>. People who can't work the shift are
            left out with the reason, for example they don't work that position, already have a shift then,
            are off, or have said they can't work at that time. Everyone else is ranked so those who won't go
            over their weekly maximum, will get a proper rest between shifts and still need hours this week
            come first. Each suggestion says why, and you can still choose anyone by hand.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            On an existing shift, <strong>Open up for cover</strong> takes the person off and offers the shift
            to others, and <strong>Remove</strong> deletes it.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Drafts and publishing">
        <FluentText>
            New shifts and changes are drafts. Staff can't see them until you publish. When you're ready,
            select <strong>Publish</strong>. The button shows how many changes are waiting.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>Published shifts appear on each person's My Shifts straight away.</li>
            <li>Each person gets one email listing just their own changes.</li>
            <li>Open shifts are offered to everyone who could work them.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Copy last week</strong> (or <strong>Copy from 4 weeks earlier</strong> in the month view)
            copies every shift in as drafts. Anyone who already has a shift at the same time is skipped.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Auto-building the rota">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Auto-build</strong> fills the week or month you're looking at from this location's
            <a href="/manage/rota/templates">shift templates</a> and picks who works each shift.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Auto-build</strong>. It lists every shift it would add, day by day, with who it picked and why,
                and which shifts it would leave open.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Add</strong> to add them as drafts, or <strong>Cancel</strong> to change nothing.</li>
            <li>Check the rota, change anything you like, then <strong>Publish</strong> as usual. Nobody sees the shifts before then.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>How it picks people:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>Only people at this location who hold the shift's position, have its required training and aren't already
                working or booked off then.</li>
            <li>Never someone who has said they can't work at that time, would go over their weekly maximum, would get less than
                11 hours' rest between shifts, or has asked for that day off. A shift nobody can take is added as an
                <strong>open shift</strong>, which you can fill by hand or staff can pick up once it's published.</li>
            <li>The rest are ranked the same way as <strong>Suggest staff</strong>: people who need shifts for their contract
                first, then people who'd rather work then, then whoever has the fewest hours that week. Shifts that only a
                few people can work are filled first.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Shifts already on the rota are never moved or removed. A shift with the same position, start and end as a
            template counts towards it, so running Auto-build again only adds what's still missing. Days already over are skipped.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Reading the rota">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Draft</strong>: staff can't see it yet.</li>
            <li><strong>Published</strong>, and <strong>Changed since publishing</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Removed</strong>: staff are told on the next publish.</li>
            <li><strong>Time off</strong> and <strong>Time off asked for</strong>.</li>
            <li>A warning icon means the person's contract isn't met that week, and a graduation cap means
                they're missing the position's required training.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
